WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:05.202
Ivy blinked. Her cabinmates were grinning at her.

2
00:00:05.203 --> 00:00:11.146
"I love your song!" Clara said. "It's so catchy!"

3
00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:15.653
"I can't believe you wrote it so fast," Willow said.

4
00:00:15.654 --> 00:00:18.912
"You're super talented, Ivy!"

5
00:00:18.913 --> 00:00:24.951
Ivy was stunned. "You mean you . . . like it?"

6
00:00:24.952 --> 00:00:31.149
"We love it!" Clara said. "Our act will be amazing!"

7
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:36.441
Willow beamed. "You really came through for us. Thanks!

8
00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:39.896
I'll start working on our dance moves."

9
00:00:39.897 --> 00:00:43.226
"Huh," Ivy thought in surprise.

10
00:00:43.227 --> 00:00:48.874
"I guess I should add songwriter to my list of talents."

11
00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:54.402
*** That afternoon the girls found an empty room where they could

12
00:00:54.403 --> 00:00:57.453
rehearse. Willow taught them the dance

13
00:00:57.454 --> 00:01:02.849
routine. She swirled and dipped, stomped her feet, and clapped her

14
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.332
hands. Clara followed her every

15
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:11.102
move. Ivy tried to keep up, but dancing was harder than it

16
00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:15.641
looked. She turned the wrong way and bumped into

17
00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:22.616
Clara. "Ivy, you're a little behind," Willow said. "Let's try that again."

18
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:35.948
Ivy sighed as the girls started over again.

19
00:01:35.949 --> 00:01:39.591
When the song was over, the girls heard clapping.

20
00:01:39.592 --> 00:01:44.398
They turned to see Private and Penelope watching them from the doorway.

21
00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:50.457
"What a great act!" Penelope said. "I'm so proud of you!"

22
00:01:50.458 --> 00:01:55.139
Private nodded. "I don't know much about popular music acts.

23
00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:01.522
But that is a peppy tune. Keep up the hard work."

24
00:02:01.523 --> 00:02:10.050
"Wow!" Willow said. "Even Private likes our act. I know we will win the talent show."

25
00:02:10.051 --> 00:02:14.417
Clara nodded. "The talent show is just the start.

26
00:02:14.418 --> 00:02:18.573
We could be the world's next big pop stars!"

27
00:02:18.574 --> 00:02:24.224
Ivy rolled her eyes. "We're not that good."

28
00:02:24.225 --> 00:02:27.771
But a little smile crept over her face.

29
00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:31.500
She pictured an arena with the three of them onstage.

30
00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:37.812
Lights blazed. A huge crowd clapped and cheered for the songs that she wrote.

31
00:02:37.813 --> 00:02:41.686
"I could be rich one day," Ivy thought.

32
00:02:41.687 --> 00:02:45.115
"I could buy all the art supplies I wanted.

33
00:02:45.116 --> 00:02:48.177
I could even have my own art studio, and—"

34
00:02:48.178 --> 00:02:51.383
"Let's keep rehearsing," Willow said.

35
00:02:51.384 --> 00:02:55.214
Willow's voice had snapped Ivy out of her daydream.

36
00:02:55.215 --> 00:03:01.466
"Every step needs to be perfect. Right, Ivy?" Willow was looking at her.

37
00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:07.217
Ivy nodded. "Right. Let's do it!"

38
00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:11.828
*** The next day Ivy left the assembly hall with Clara and

39
00:03:11.829 --> 00:03:14.620
Willow. They planned to rehearse all

40
00:03:14.621 --> 00:03:19.526
morning. Then Ivy saw Ezra by himself. He looked

41
00:03:19.527 --> 00:03:23.252
upset. "I'll be right back," Ivy

42
00:03:23.253 --> 00:03:25.701
said. She hurried over to

43
00:03:25.702 --> 00:03:30.612
Ezra. "Where's Glen? Shouldn't you two be working on your act with

44
00:03:30.613 --> 00:03:35.289
Wes?" Ezra frowned. "Glen has been acting so

45
00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.624
weird. He says he can't participate in the talent show

46
00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:44.154
anymore. He's too busy being Camp Evergreen's number-one

47
00:03:44.155 --> 00:03:48.638
leader. So I guess Wes and I have to do the act without him."

48
00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:54.923
Ivy tried to cheer up Ezra. "Maybe that will be better," she joked.

49
00:03:54.924 --> 00:04:01.457
"Better than getting booed offstage because of Glen's terrible knock-knock jokes!"

50
00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:06.823
"It's not better, Ivy! Wes hardly ever speaks!

51
00:04:06.824 --> 00:04:11.992
How can we do a comedy act together?" Ezra hung his head.

52
00:04:11.993 --> 00:04:15.440
"I might be able to write a few jokes.

53
00:04:15.441 --> 00:04:23.745
But I can't get onstage without Glen. I'm too nervous. I don't know what to do."

54
00:04:23.746 --> 00:04:29.401
"Talk to Glen again," she said. "Ask him to write the comedy act."

55
00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:33.862
"You don't get it," Ezra said. "He—"

56
00:04:33.863 --> 00:04:36.553
The PA system crackled loudly.

57
00:04:36.554 --> 00:04:40.541
Then a familiar voice blared through the speakers.

58
00:04:40.542 --> 00:04:44.752
"Greetings, campers. It's your lucky day.

59
00:04:44.753 --> 00:04:54.550
Today's hike will be led by me—Glen, Camp Evergreen's amazing, fantastic, number-one leader.

60
00:04:54.551 --> 00:05:02.209
My assistant Larry and I will meet you in the square in ten minutes. Don't be late."

